{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"grp_writer","type":"group","x":200,"y":1400,"width":2220,"height":1580,"color":"5","label":"Literature Review Studio & Thesis Writer"},
		{"id":"grp_library","type":"group","x":-3160,"y":1000,"width":2260,"height":1180,"color":"6","label":"Reference Manager & Central Library (F-17)"},
		{"id":"grp_guardrails","type":"group","x":-3225,"y":-480,"width":2000,"height":930,"color":"1","label":"Stopping Fake Citations: 3-Tier Guardrails (F-16)"},
		{"id":"grp_ingest","type":"group","x":-950,"y":-1200,"width":1830,"height":860,"color":"2","label":"Fixing PDF Ingestion"},
		{"id":"grp_router","type":"group","x":200,"y":200,"width":1650,"height":850,"color":"3","label":"Query Router: Cutting Token Waste"},
		{"id":"grp_vector","type":"group","x":720,"y":-2080,"width":1250,"height":720,"color":"5","label":"Vector Storage: ChromaDB Local"},
		{"id":"start_goal","type":"text","text":"### Start: The basic goal\nWe wanted to upload research papers, ask questions about them, and get reliable answers with exact page citations for our FYP thesis.\n","x":-2200,"y":-1360,"width":480,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"start_code_att1","type":"text","text":"### Day 1: Simple LangChain attempt\n```python\n# backend/ingestion/pdf_parser.py\nfrom langchain_community.document_loaders import PyPDFLoader\n\nloader = PyPDFLoader(pdf_path)\ndocuments = loader.load()\n# Slow (3s per paper) and broke on academic layouts\n```\n","x":-2400,"y":-970,"width":480,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"prob_layout","type":"text","text":"### Problem 1: 2-column papers broke\nAcademic papers use two columns.\nStandard loaders read across the page horizontally:\n`Column 1 Line 1 + Column 2 Line 1`\nResult was completely scrambled sentences.\n","x":-1680,"y":-1140,"width":420,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"prob_hallucinate","type":"text","text":"### Problem 2: Made-up page numbers\nThe model claimed:\n*\"Vaswani reported 44.2 BLEU on page 84\"*\nThe paper was only 12 pages long.\nIf you cite a fake page in a thesis defense, you fail.\n","x":-1680,"y":-820,"width":420,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"why_local_chroma","type":"text","text":"### Why local ChromaDB instead of Pinecone?\n- **Privacy:** Unpublished thesis findings stay on the laptop. No third-party cloud leaks.\n- **Cost:** $0. Pinecone charges monthly.\n- **Offline:** Works in university labs with zero internet.\n","x":760,"y":-2020,"width":460,"height":170,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"chroma_filters","type":"text","text":"### Metadata isolation & distance filter\n```python\n# Tenant isolation per user & workspace\nwhere = {\n    \"$and\": [\n        {\"user_id\": current_user.id},\n        {\"doc_name\": {\"$in\": workspace_docs}}\n    ]\n}\n\n# Distance filter: drop irrelevant chunks\nif chunk.distance > 0.75:\n    drop_chunk()\n```\n","x":1360,"y":-2020,"width":480,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c10ca722a83ad3d1","type":"text","text":"","x":1492,"y":-1971,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"chroma_code","type":"text","text":"### ChromaDB batched upsert\n```python\n# backend/embeddings/vector_store.py\n# SQLite crashes if you pass >999 parameters at once\n# So we batch upsert in groups of 500\nbatch_size = 500\nfor i in range(0, len(chunks), batch_size):\n    batch = chunks[i : i + batch_size]\n    collection.upsert(\n        ids=[c.metadata[\"chunk_id\"] for c in batch],\n        documents=[c.page_content for c in batch],\n        metadatas=[c.metadata for c in batch]\n    )\n```\n","x":760,"y":-1740,"width":460,"height":290,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"fix_mupdf_code","type":"text","text":"### PyMuPDF block sorting\n```python\n# backend/ingestion/pipeline.py\nimport pymupdf\n\ndoc = pymupdf.open(pdf_path)\nfor page in doc:\n    # sort=True orders blocks top-to-bottom, left-to-right\n    blocks = page.get_text(\"blocks\", sort=True)\n    text = \"\n\".join(b[4].strip() for b in blocks if b[6] == 0)\n```\nPreserves two-column reading order and runs 15x faster.\n","x":-900,"y":-1140,"width":520,"height":270,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"fix_summary_cache","type":"text","text":"### Summary cache on upload\n```python\n# summary_worker.py\n# On upload, background worker extracts Intro + Conclusion\n# and stores an executive summary in SQLite\ncached_summary = generate_summary(pages[0], pages[-1])\n```\nWhen user asks *\"what is this paper about?\"*:\nReturns from cache in **<50ms with 0 LLM tokens burned**.\n","x":140,"y":-1080,"width":460,"height":240,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"guard_prompt_fail","type":"text","text":"### Why prompting alone failed\nWe told the LLM: *\"Only cite real pages from the context\"*.\nIt still hallucinated page numbers because LLMs are autocomplete engines.\nWhen caught, the model argued that page 84 was real.\n**Conclusion: We needed deterministic python code to verify citations.**\n","x":-3175,"y":-330,"width":460,"height":180,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ss_placeholder_pdf_nav","type":"text","text":"### [Screenshot placeholder: PDF Page Jump]\nPaste screenshot here showing:\n- Clicking citation badge jumps split-screen viewer to page 4\n- Text highlighted in yellow\n","x":-1885,"y":-440,"width":480,"height":220,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"router_fuzzy_code","type":"text","text":"### Fuzzy target document matching\n```python\n# Handles typos and @mentions\n# e.g. '@attention' or 'transformer' matches 'Attention_Is_All_You_Need.pdf'\nclean_query = re.sub(r\"[`'\"\\/,;:()<>{}[\\]@]\", \" \", query_lower)\nfor doc in available_docs:\n    pattern = r\"\b\" + re.escape(doc.replace(\".pdf\", \"\")) + r\"\b\"\n    if re.search(pattern, clean_query):\n        matched.add(doc)\n```\n","x":750,"y":570,"width":520,"height":250,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ss_placeholder_router","type":"text","text":"### [Screenshot placeholder: Router]\nPaste screenshot here showing:\n- Terminal output of fast-path cache hit\n- Chat response showing instant reply with 0 tokens\n","x":1310,"y":690,"width":500,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"fix_title_hack","type":"text","text":"### Finding paper titles without clean filenames\nFiles are often named `2305.18290v2.pdf` or `main(1).pdf`.\n```python\n# bibliographic_extractor.py\n# Scan Page 1 font spans: text with size >= 14pt is the title\nif span[\"size\"] >= 14 and len(span[\"text\"]) > 10:\n    paper_title = span[\"text\"]\n```\nFalls back to PDF metadata, then to cleaned filename.\n","x":-920,"y":-710,"width":520,"height":240,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ss_placeholder_ingest","type":"text","text":"### [Screenshot placeholder: Ingestion]\nPaste screenshot here showing:\n- Extracted paper title in UI\n- Terminal log showing PyMuPDF parsing time (<200ms)\n","x":-200,"y":-710,"width":460,"height":150,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"lib_why","type":"text","text":"### Why a Reference Manager?\nA chat session is temporary.\nWhen writing an FYP thesis, you have 30 to 50 papers across different chapters.\nWe needed a permanent Zotero-style library with metadata, tags, and BibTeX export.\n","x":-2790,"y":1070,"width":460,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"router_problem","type":"text","text":"### Why we needed a router\n- User types *\"hello\"* ➔ naive RAG ran vector search and burned 2,000 tokens.\n- Comparing Paper A (10 pages) & Paper B (60 pages) ➔ Paper B took all 8 chunks; Paper A got zero chunks (document starvation).\n","x":250,"y":270,"width":460,"height":180,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ss_placeholder_library","type":"text","text":"### [Screenshot placeholder: Library 3-Pane View]\nPaste screenshot here showing:\n- Left pane: Workspace collections & tags\n- Center pane: Sortable paper list with titles & authors\n- Right pane: Inspector drawer with metadata & BibTeX copy\n","x":-1534,"y":1070,"width":520,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"fig_pdf_viewer_card","type":"file","file":"assets/Pdf_Viewer.png","x":-1500,"y":1370,"width":560,"height":670,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"lib_bibtex_code","type":"text","text":"### 1-Click BibTeX export\n```python\n# backend/ingestion/citation_engine.py\n# Formats clean bibtex entries with unique citekeys\nentry = f\"@article{{{citekey},\n  author = {{{authors}}},\n  title = {{{title}}},\n  year = {{{year}}}\n}}\"\n```\nOne-click download of `references.bib` for Overleaf / LaTeX thesis writing.\n","x":-2280,"y":1635,"width":560,"height":325,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"lib_doi_code","type":"text","text":"### Auto-fetching metadata via DOI / arXiv\n```python\n# backend/ingestion/identifier_resolver.py\nDOI_PATTERN = re.compile(r'\b10\\.\\d{4,9}/[-._;()/:A-Za-z0-9]+\b')\nARXIV_PATTERN = re.compile(r'\b(?:arxiv:\\s*)?(\\d{4}\\.\\d{4,5})\b')\n\n# Queries CrossRef REST API for DOIs\n# Queries arXiv Atom API for preprints\n# Fetches: Title, Authors, Year, Journal/Venue, Abstract\n```\nAlso downloads open-access PDF automatically via Unpaywall API.\n","x":-3020,"y":1500,"width":460,"height":420,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"router_perdoc_code","type":"text","text":"### Fair multi-paper retrieval\n```python\n# backend/rag/retriever.py\n# Pull equal chunks from every target document\nretrieved_chunks = []\nfor doc in target_docs:\n    doc_results = search_similar_chunks(\n        query=query, \n        top_k=per_doc_k, \n        doc_names=[doc]\n    )\n    retrieved_chunks.extend(doc_results)\n```\nGuarantees both papers get fair representation in the prompt.\n","x":750,"y":270,"width":520,"height":270,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"guard_t1_code","type":"text","text":"### Tier 1: Input Rails (Adversarial defense)\n```python\n# backend/guardrails/input_rails.py\n# Blocks prompt injection in 0.1ms with 0 tokens burned\nfor pattern in INJECTION_PATTERNS:\n    if re.search(pattern, query, re.IGNORECASE):\n        return GuardrailResult(action=RailAction.BLOCK)\n\n# Redact exposed API keys before sending to LLM\nquery = re.sub(r\"AIza[0-9A-Za-z-_]{35}\", \"[REDACTED_KEY]\", query)\n```\n","x":-3175,"y":-110,"width":460,"height":250,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"guard_t3_code","type":"text","text":"### Tier 3: Output Rails (Citation Provenance Check)\n```python\n# backend/guardrails/output_rails.py\n# 1. Build ground-truth set of actual retrieved (doc, page) pairs\nground_truth = {\n    (chunk['doc_name'].lower(), chunk['page_number'])\n    for chunk in retrieved_chunks\n}\n\n# 2. Cross-reference every [Doc, p.X] citation generated by the LLM\nfor cite in extracted_citations:\n    pair = (cite['doc_name'].lower(), cite['page_number'])\n    if pair in ground_truth:\n        cite['verified'] = True   # Blue badge in UI\n    else:\n        cite['verified'] = False  # Amber [Unverified] badge!\n        hallucinated_count += 1\n```\n","x":-2655,"y":-330,"width":580,"height":360,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"fig_rag_diagram","type":"file","file":"assets/act_rag.png","x":-1723,"y":-70,"width":417,"height":480,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"guard_t2_code","type":"text","text":"### Tier 2: Retrieval Rails (Token budget)\n```python\n# backend/guardrails/retrieval_rails.py\n# Hard context cap at 4,200 tokens\n# Leaves room so Groq's 6,000 TPM limit never crashes\nif total_tokens + chunk_tokens > 4200:\n    break\n```\n","x":-3175,"y":180,"width":460,"height":180,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"lit_studio_code","type":"text","text":"### 5-Stage Monograph generation\n```python\n# backend/rag/literature_review.py\n# Stage 1: Outline generation (Foundations, Taxonomy, Synthesis, Benchmarks, Gaps)\n# Stage 2: Draft sections (600-900 words per section)\n# Stage 3: Comparative matrix table\n# Stage 4: Conclusion & research roadmap\n# Stage 5: Markdown / Word export\n```\n","x":250,"y":1470,"width":480,"height":350,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"fig_router_chart","type":"file","file":"assets/Query_Classification.png","x":1310,"y":270,"width":499,"height":329,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"router_heuristics_code","type":"text","text":"### Fast-path heuristics (0 tokens, <1ms)\n```python\n# backend/rag/router.py\nlowered = query.lower().strip()\n\n# Greetings\nif re.search(r\"^(hi|hello|hey)\b\", lowered):\n    return direct_response() # 0 LLM calls\n\n# Catalog queries\nif \"how many papers\" in lowered or \"list files\" in lowered:\n    return get_workspace_catalog() # Direct SQL query\n\n# Single-paper summary\nif is_summary_query and len(target_docs) == 1:\n    return get_cached_summary(target_docs[0]) # From cache\n```\nSaves ~35% of all LLM calls.\n","x":250,"y":480,"width":460,"height":360,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"lit_matrix_sample","type":"text","text":"### Automated comparative matrix\n| Paper | Method | Benchmark | Metric | Limitation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Vaswani 2017 | Self-Attention | WMT14 | 28.4 BLEU | O(N^2) memory |\n| Devlin 2018 | Masked LM | GLUE | 80.5% GLUE | Unidirectional |\n| Lewis 2020 | RAG | TriviaQA | SOTA QA | Hallucinations |\n","x":340,"y":2600,"width":680,"height":320,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"lit_rolling_code","type":"text","text":"### Rolling memory prevents repetition\n```python\n# Each section draft receives a summary of previous sections\ndraft_prompt = f\"\"\"\nPREVIOUS SECTIONS SUMMARY:\n{rolling_memory}\n\nEVIDENCE FROM PAPERS:\n{context_block}\n\nWrite Section {sec_num}: {sec_title}\nDo not repeat points already discussed above.\n\"\"\"\n```\n","x":250,"y":1950,"width":480,"height":410,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"writer_code","type":"text","text":"### Live thesis writer & citation drawer\n```javascript\n// frontend/src/components/writer/LibraryCitationDrawer.jsx\n// Press Ctrl+Shift+C -> select paper -> clicks 'Insert Citation'\n// Inserts [1] (IEEE) or (Vaswani, 2017) (APA) into draft\n// Automatically updates the References section at bottom of draft\n```\n","x":1030,"y":1470,"width":520,"height":350,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ss_placeholder_writer","type":"text","text":"### [Screenshot placeholder: Document Writer]\nPaste screenshot here showing:\n- Split-screen thesis draft editor\n- Citation drawer open on the right\n- In-text citation `[1]` inserted with live References list updated\n","x":900,"y":1870,"width":520,"height":220,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"fig_matrix_diagram","type":"file","file":"assets/act_matrix.png","x":1500,"y":1900,"width":887,"height":980,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"ss_placeholder_badge","type":"text","text":"### [Screenshot placeholder: Verified Citation Badge]\nPaste screenshot here showing:\n- Blue `[Paper.pdf, p. 4]` badge in chat\n- Amber `[Unverified]` badge when a page is fake\n- Grounding ratio score at bottom of message\n","x":-2645,"y":180,"width":580,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"lib_unionfind_code","type":"text","text":"### Duplicate detection using Union-Find\n```python\n# backend/ingestion/duplicate_detector.py\n# Problem: User uploads 'attention.pdf', '1706.03762.pdf', 'vaswani.pdf'\nclass UnionFind:\n    def __init__(self, elements):\n        self.parent = {el: el for el in elements}\n    def find(self, i):\n        if self.parent[i] == i: return i\n        self.parent[i] = self.find(self.parent[i]) # Path compression\n        return self.parent[i]\n    def union(self, i, j):\n        root_i, root_j = self.find(i), self.find(j)\n        if root_i != root_j: self.parent[root_i] = root_j\n```\nGroups duplicate papers and merges notes, tags, and workspace links.\n","x":-2180,"y":1065,"width":560,"height":490,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cc7518e63ee77bc5","x":-2853,"y":-1088,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":""}
